The work in this directory is a re-implementation and adaptation, not a copy of
the original source tree. It was produced by reading the upstream Python sources
and rewriting the behaviour in TypeScript for the DeepSeek Harness plugin API.
The following classes of change were made; every one of them is also marked in
the affected source file with a `DEVIATION` comment explaining the reason.

Rewritten / translated
  - Every Python module ported to TypeScript: `gpt_researcher/agent.py`,
    `actions/`, `skills/`, `config/`, `context/`, `prompts.py`, `retrievers/`,
    `scraper/`, `document/`, `memory/`, `vector_store/`, `utils/`, and the
    `multi_agents/` LangGraph flow.
  - Prompt templates were copied verbatim and are byte-compared against the
    upstream renderings by the test suite.

Structural changes required by the host
  - I/O is injected (`EngineDeps`: llm, http, env, log, progress, signal).
    There are no provider SDK imports and no direct `process.env` credential
    reads.
  - LangGraph is replaced by a sequential async driver with the same node order
    and the same conditional review/revision loop, explicitly bounded.
  - Progress events that upstream streams over a websocket are forwarded as
    DeepSeek Harness deferred-context messages.
  - Cost accounting uses the host's reported token usage and falls back to a
    character-based estimate (no bundled tokeniser).

Reduced scope (fails loudly instead of degrading silently)
  - No MCP client (the host provides MCP natively).
  - No headless-browser scraper; the `browser` scraper reports that it is not
    bundled.
  - Server-backed vector stores and non-bundled LLM/embedding providers report
    the working alternatives.
  - PDF extraction is limited to uncompressed content streams.
  - Image generation is not ported.

Fixed upstream defects
  - `DeepResearchSkill.process_research_results` split `Learning [url]: text` on
    the first colon (inside `https:`), corrupting every extracted learning. This
    port takes the text after the `[citation]` group.
  - `ContextCompressor`'s JSON repair helpers rewrote text inside string values
    (`"The value is True"` became `"The value is true"`) and could invalidate
    their own repairs. The repair pass is now string-state aware.
  - `trim_context_to_word_limit` semantics: the port keeps upstream's truncating
    branch, which the pinned checkout implements but an earlier revision of this
    port dropped, leaving a single oversized page to empty the whole context.
  - `ContextCompressor`'s nearest-chunk fallback and the report generator's empty
    context handling are described below.

Safety and robustness deltas (additions, not ports)
  - Fetch policy: non-http(s) schemes, loopback, RFC1918, link-local/cloud
    metadata, CGNAT, ULA and internal names are refused unless
    `allowPrivateHosts` is set; redirects are validated hop by hop; search domain
    filters must be hostnames. Upstream fetches any URL it is given.
  - Deep-research `breadth`/`depth`/`concurrency` are clamped (10/4/16) because
    they arrive as model-supplied tool arguments.
  - Progress events are throttled to milestones: upstream streams every event to
    a websocket, while a deferred context here becomes a durable user-role
    message the model re-reads.
  - `gptr_quick_search` with a summary performs one search, not two.
  - Vector-store cosine similarity raises a typed error on a dimension mismatch
    instead of silently comparing truncated vectors, and a corrupt persisted
    entry no longer destroys the rest of the durable store.
  - Cancellation propagates end to end (model calls, HTTP, worker pools and the
    report ladders) instead of degrading into a successful empty result.
  - When no sources were gathered, `write_report` returns an explicit abstention
    rather than prompting the model for a report it cannot ground. This is a
    deliberate behavioural difference from upstream, which writes the report
    anyway.

Upstream behaviours that are preserved deliberately, including quirks
  - `SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD` defaults to 0.35 (shadowing the config's 0.42);
    `COMPRESSION_THRESHOLD` fast path at 8 000 characters; the seed search uses
    only `retrievers[0]` while URL harvesting uses all non-MCP retrievers;
    `curate_sources` uses strict JSON parsing and returns the original data on
    failure; visited URLs are never cleared between runs.
